<title>USA: Iowa-So Minn hogs actual Friday 104,000 - USDA.</title>
<headline>Iowa-So Minn hogs actual Friday 104,000 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA said Friday's actual Iowa and southern Minnesota marketings were 104,000 head versus the estimate of 105,000 and Saturday's actual was 13,000 versus the estimate of 10,000. Opening trade not well established.  Early sales Barrows and Gilts steady to $0.50 per cwt higher than the mid-session Friday.</p>
<p>US 1-3   46-49% Carcass Base Lean*  Country	   Plants</p>
<p>220-260 lbs		  52.00 -53.50	   53.00 -54.50</p>
<p>few			    51.00 -51.50 &amp; 54.00 52.50</p>
<p>Sows:  mostly steady to 2.00 higher.</p>
<p>US 1-3     300-450 lbs.  42.50 -45.00	   43.00 -45.00</p>
<p>450-500 lbs.		 46.00 -48.00	   46.00 -48.00</p>
<p>500 lbs. up		  48.00 -52.00	   48.00 -53.00</p>
